'''Els Horts''' is a municipality in the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 60,624 in 2026, it is a semi-rural suburban district situated between the dense commuter hub of [[Enllaç]] and the agricultural lands of the southern comarca. The municipality combines residential development along its northern edge with active farmland and orchards across its southern and western areas, reflecting its name ({{lang|ca|els horts}}, "the orchards").

== Geography ==

Els Horts occupies a transitional position between the built-up Enllaç corridor and the open agricultural lands of southern Cumará. The terrain is gently undulating, with elevations ranging from approximately 50 to 120 metres. Several small streams cross the municipality, draining westward toward the coastal river system. The soil is fertile and well-suited for fruit and vegetable cultivation, which historically gave the area its name.

=== Climate ===

Els Horts has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} ({{w|Köppen climate classification|Köppen}} Am), with average daily highs of 30 to 32 °C and lows of 22 to 24 °C. The wet season extends from May to November, with annual precipitation averaging approximately 2,200 mm.

== Demographics ==

Els Horts's population of 60,624 is split between the residential northern fringe, which forms part of the Enllaç commuter belt, and the agricultural southern area, where the population is more dispersed. [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboans]] constitute the largest group, with a significant mixed Balboan population. The [[Fosian Balboan|Fosian]] community is small.

== Economy ==

The economy of Els Horts combines commuter residential services with agriculture. The northern residential areas provide housing for workers commuting to [[Enllaç]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], and the [[International City of Areza]]. The southern and western areas retain active farmland producing fruits, vegetables, and maize for the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan market. Small-scale food processing and agricultural supply businesses operate along the main road corridors.

== Transport ==

[[CristoCarril]] [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] serves Els Horts via the [[Els Horts (CristoCarril)|Els Horts station]], providing a commuter rail connection northward to [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal|Sant Cristòfor Central]] through the Enllaç corridor. Local roads connect the municipality to [[Enllaç]] and the neighbouring Cumará communities.

